    "The capture contains several programs (an unnamed program ending with SSC 460, BA in Sociology, BA in Supply Chain Management, and the start of BS in Computer Software Technology); the request did not name one, so this ledger assumes the BA in Supply Chain Management. Please confirm the intended program.",
    "Overlap: 6 credits from the major (ECO 204 and INF 220, both marked *) also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements. The capture does not say which specific Foundations requirements they replace. Listed blocks total 126 credits (33 + 39 + 54) against the 120-credit total.",
    "The Global Campus Foundations block is kept as a single 33-credit requirement. The standard sequence lists individual courses, but it states that courses may be substituted, and the program-specific mapping is not given.",
    "For this program, TEC 100 Computer Literacy replaces GEN 102. The capture does not print TEC 100's credits.",
    "GEN 101 is scheduled first and satisfies 3 elective credits. Students transferring fewer than 30 credits also take GEN 104, which satisfies 3 elective credits. Neither course's placement within the 54 elective credits is itemized.",
    "Graduation policies not itemized as courses: a minimum of 30 credits completed at the University (residency); a minimum of 30 upper-division credits, including 18 upper-division credits in the major; a 2.00 minimum cumulative GPA.",
    "BUS 401, BUS 308 and BUS 307 require that the Quantitative Reasoning requirement be met first. The capture does not define which course satisfies Quantitative Reasoning.",
    "SCM 499 must be taken last in the program."
